  "question": "1) Background / Context\nThe project involves implementing a two-factor authentication system for Django applications, enhancing security by requiring additional steps beyond the standard username and password. This solution builds upon Django's existing authentication frameworks, specifically `django-otp` and `django.contrib.auth`, providing seamless integration into Django projects.\n\n2) Objectives\nThe objective is to develop a comprehensive two-factor authentication feature that supports multiple authentication methods. Users should be able to authenticate via phone call, SMS, token generator apps like Google Authenticator, or a YubiKey hardware token.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Users: Individuals requiring secure access to Django-based applications.\n- Administrators: Manage the security settings and user access control within the system.\n- Developers: Integrate and maintain the two-factor authentication feature in various Django projects.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n- User Authentication: Allow users to authenticate using:\n  - Phone call\n  - Text messages (SMS)\n  - Token generator apps (e.g., Google Authenticator)\n  - YubiKey (optional)\n- Integration: Ensure compatibility and effortless integration with Django's authentication framework and `django-otp`.\n- Account Management: Administrators can monitor and configure two-factor authentication settings for users.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Security: Provide a robust authentication mechanism to protect user accounts.\n- Scalability: Support the integration into various Django projects without performance issues.\n- Usability: Deliver a user-friendly authentication experience inspired by Google’s Two-Step Authentication.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0028\nCREATE TABLE `auth_user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(150) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(128) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(254) NOT NULL,\n  `is_active` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '1',\n  `date_joined` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `auth_user_username_uniq` (`username`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `two_factor_device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `device_type` varchar(32) NOT NULL,\n  `is_confirmed` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_used_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `two_factor_device_user_id_idx` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `two_factor_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `auth_user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `phone_device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `method` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `country_code` varchar(8) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `is_primary` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `phone_device_device_id_uniq` (`device_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `phone_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `two_factor_device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `token_device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `secret_key` varchar(64) NOT NULL,\n  `digits` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '6',\n  `timestep` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '30',\n  `drift` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `token_device_device_id_uniq` (`device_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `token_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `two_factor_device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `yubikey_device` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `device_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `public_id` varchar(12) NOT NULL,\n  `secret_key` varchar(64) NOT NULL,\n  `counter` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `yubikey_device_device_id_uniq` (`device_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `yubikey_device_public_id_uniq` (`public_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `yubikey_device_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`device_id`) REFERENCES `two_factor_device` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
